From 104bf40ebb11426fe22cb5f6d1c430fbc2e1e8f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sylvain Zimmer <sylvain@sylvainzimmer.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:57:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] hostagent: relay host deletions to reverse-sshfs mounts

mountInotify did not relay host deletions, so the guest never got an
event when a file was removed on the host.

The host watcher now also listens for removals and renames. When the
path is gone, the host agent asks the reverse-sshfs mount to expect its
removal (sshocker ExpectRemove), then sends an Inotify event with the
new `removed` field. The guest agent removes the path in the guest,
which emits IN_DELETE, and the host SFTP server does nothing for that
removal, so the host keeps the path if it was created again since.

This only applies to reverse-sshfs mounts with the builtin driver on
Linux and macOS hosts. For other mounts, and for paths under a mount
nested in the guest, nothing is sent. The guest only gets an event for
files it had looked up or listed before.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Sylvain Zimmer <sylvain@sylvainzimmer.com>
